-- title:
--   Deuring's isomorphism criterion with markings and level transport
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$, and let $X_0$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose $\kappa$-points $P$ with $q'P=0$ are zero. Let $\Lambda\subseteq\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of the rational quaternion algebra with parameters $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ which contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans the algebra over $\mathbb Q$ and is finitely generated, and let $\theta$ be an injective ring homomorphism from the subring $\mathrm{rationalEndSubring}\ \kappa\ X_0$ (the subring of additive endomorphisms of the $\kappa$-points of $X_0$ generated by the $\kappa$-rationally represented endomorphisms, together with $0$) onto $\Lambda$. Let $W,W',W_1,W_1'$ be elliptic Weierstrass curves over $\kappa$ and let $\chi\colon X_0\to W$, $\chi'\colon X_0\to W'$, $\psi\colon W\to W_1$, $\psi'\colon W'\to W_1'$ be nonzero additive maps on points lying in the respective sets $\mathrm{rationalHomSet}$, i.e. each is either $0$ or given, off a finite set of $x$-coordinates, by a fixed quadruple of bivariate polynomials over $\kappa$ in the two coordinates. For a map $\varphi$ out of $X_0$ write $K(\varphi)$ for its kernel ideal set, the set of elements of $\mathrm{rationalEndSubring}\ \kappa\ X_0$ of the form $\rho\circ\varphi$ with $\rho$ in the rational hom set from the target of $\varphi$ to $X_0$. Assume that for one nonzero $c\in\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ both $\theta(K(\chi'))=\theta(K(\chi))\,c$ and $\theta(K(\psi'\circ\chi'))=\theta(K(\psi\circ\chi))\,c$. Then there are $\varphi$ in the rational hom set from $W$ to $W'$ and $\varphi'$ in that from $W'$ to $W$ with $\varphi'\circ\varphi=\mathrm{id}$ and $\varphi\circ\varphi'=\mathrm{id}$, such that moreover there exist a nonzero natural number $n$ and $\gamma_0\in\mathrm{rationalEndSubring}\ \kappa\ X_0$ with $\theta(\gamma_0)=n\,c$ and $\varphi\circ\chi\circ\gamma_0=n\,\chi'$, and $\varphi$ carries $\ker\psi$ into $\ker\psi'$.
--
--   This is Deuring's isomorphism criterion in the form needed for level structures: two markings $\chi,\chi'$ of a supersingular curve whose kernel ideals lie in the same right class, with the same right multiplier $c$ at level one and at level $\psi$, have isomorphic targets, and the isomorphism is pinned relative to the markings up to the scalar $n$ and transports the kernel of the auxiliary isogeny. It feeds the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison between ideal classes of a quaternion order and pairs consisting of a supersingular curve with a subgroup, in particular the counting and injectivity statements for level Hecke sets.
